```

- Order: input port order, then element order within each input. Shallow: elements are copied by reference, nested arrays aren't flattened, and duplicates are kept.
- Single values: text, numbers, booleans, and objects on an input are added as one element. `null` (the default for an unset JSON input) adds nothing.
- Cap: at most 10,000 elements; extra elements are dropped with one warning per restart per loop index through `ctx.services.log("warn", …)`.
- Immutability: a new array every frame; never mutate an input. Push elements in chunks (not one giant spread) to avoid call-stack limits on large inputs.
- Frame 0: evaluates with authored values; no special case.
- Loops: evaluates once per loop index. Looped inputs zip into a loop of joined arrays (longest wins, shorter loops wrap, scalars broadcast). It never gathers a loop into an array; that's Loop to Array.
- Muted: Array passes Array 1 through, per the default bypass.
- Restart and dispose: restart clears the warn-once flag. Nothing to release.
- Coming from Origami: Origami starts with 2 unnamed inputs and one unnamed output; importers map inputs in order to `array1…`. Origami doesn't document single-value inputs; Sonobe adds them as one element.

