Helpers:
```
const MISSING = Symbol("missing");
function rank(v) { return v === MISSING ? 6 : v === null ? 0 : typeof v === "boolean" ? 1 : typeof v === "number" ? 2 : typeof v === "string" ? 3 : Array.isArray(v) ? 4 : 5; }
function compare(a, b) { // ascending
  const r = rank(a) - rank(b);
  if (r !== 0) return r;
  if (typeof a === "boolean") return a === b ? 0 : a ? 1 : -1;
  if (typeof a === "number") return a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0;
  if (typeof a === "string") {
    const la = a.toLowerCase(), lb = b.toLowerCase();
    if (la !== lb) return la < lb ? -1 : 1;
    return a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0; // same letters: uppercase code units first
  }
  return 0; // null, arrays, objects tie
}
```

Each frame:
```
const array = ctx.input("array");
if (!Array.isArray(array)) { if (array !== null) warnOnce("Array isn't a JSON array, so Array Sort outputs []"); ctx.output("output", []); return; }
const key = ctx.input<string>("key");
const descending = ctx.input<string>("sortBy") === "descending";
const sortValue = (item) => key === "" ? item : isPlainObject(item) && Object.hasOwn(item, key) ? item[key] : MISSING;
const decorated = array.map((item, i) => ({ item, v: sortValue(item), i }));
decorated.sort((x, y) => {
  const xm = x.v === MISSING, ym = y.v === MISSING;
  if (xm || ym) return xm === ym ? x.i - y.i : xm ? 1 : -1; // missing last in both directions
  const c = descending ? -compare(x.v, y.v) : compare(x.v, y.v);
  return c !== 0 ? c : x.i - y.i; // ties keep original order
});
ctx.output("output", decorated.map((d) => d.item));
```

- Text: code-unit comparison of `toLowerCase()`, with ties broken by exact code units. No locale collation and no natural number ordering, so results are identical in every host. Accented letters sort after z.
- Stability: ties keep input order in both directions; Descending is not the same as reversing Ascending.
- Key: exact, case-sensitive, top-level only (no dot paths). A present `null` field sorts as `null`, before booleans; a missing field or a non-object element sorts after everything.
- Immutability: sort a copy; elements are copied by reference.
- Non-arrays: `null` outputs `[]` silently; other values output `[]` and warn once per restart per loop index.
- Frame 0: evaluates with authored values; no special case.
- Loops: evaluates once per loop index; looped Sort By or Key sort the same array different ways. It never sorts a loop itself.
- Coming from Origami: Array and Sort By match Origami, whose output is unnamed. Key is a Sonobe addition; importers leave it empty. Origami doesn't document text case, mixed kinds, or stability; Sonobe defines them as above.

